        <p class="chart-caption">Figure 1: Average AI risk score rises from {risk_2015:.3f} (2015) to {risk_2035:.3f} (2035), with projection period beginning after 2024.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Risk by Job Role</h3>
    <p>Automation risk is not evenly distributed. <strong>Business Analyst</strong> roles carry the highest average risk score ({high_risk_score:.3f}), followed by <strong>Data Analyst</strong> ({ai_risk_by_job.iloc[1]:.3f}) and <strong>Software Engineer</strong> ({ai_risk_by_job.iloc[2]:.3f}). At the opposite end, <strong>AI Researcher</strong> ({low_risk_score:.3f}), <strong>Cybersecurity Analyst</strong> ({ai_risk_by_job.iloc[-2]:.3f}), and <strong>ML Engineer</strong> ({ai_risk_by_job.iloc[-3]:.3f}) demonstrate the strongest resilience.</p>

    <div class="chart-container">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['ai_risk_by_job']}" alt="AI Risk by Job Title">
        <p class="chart-caption">Figure 2: Business Analyst and Data Analyst roles sit in the high-risk zone, while AI Researcher and Cybersecurity Analyst remain firmly in low-risk territory.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Risk by Geography</h3>
    <p>Country-level differences in AI risk are relatively narrow (range: {risk_by_country.min():.3f}–{risk_by_country.max():.3f}), but directional signals matter. <strong>{highest_risk_country}</strong> records the highest average risk ({risk_by_country.iloc[0]:.3f}), potentially reflecting a higher concentration of routine-process roles in the dataset. The UK shows the lowest average risk ({risk_by_country.iloc[-1]:.3f}). These differences should be interpreted with awareness of sample composition rather than as definitive national rankings.</p>

    <h3>Risk by Experience Level</h3>
    <p>Experience provides a meaningful buffer. Senior-level roles show lower average AI risk than Entry-level positions across nearly all job families. This pattern suggests that strategic judgment, stakeholder management, and complex decision-making—capabilities typically associated with seniority—are harder to automate than execution-oriented tasks.</p>

    <div class="chart-container">
