    </div>

    <h4>Key Risk Findings</h4>
    <ul>
        <li>The top three highest-risk roles (Business Analyst, Data Analyst, Software Engineer) account for a disproportionate share of total job openings—making their exposure a systemic concern.</li>
        <li>Low-risk roles (AI Researcher, Cybersecurity Analyst, ML Engineer) are concentrated in specialized technical domains requiring deep expertise and contextual judgment.</li>
        <li>Risk acceleration is sharpest in the 2028–2035 window, suggesting that near-term workforce planning must account for rapidly shifting automation boundaries.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

